<sn><md>### Delete a specific file

```bash
rclone delete mega:Documents/file.pdf
```

Delete files matching a pattern
Delete all `.txt` files:

```bash
rclone delete mega:Documents --include "*.txt"
```
</md></sn><sn><md>### Delete empty directories

After deleting files, you can remove empty directories:

```bash
rclone rmdirs mega:Documents
```
</md></sn><sn><md>### Preview before deleting

Use `--dry-run` to see what would be deleted **without actually deleting anything**:

```bash
rclone delete mega:Documents --dry-run
```

This is highly recommended before performing a large deletion.
</md></sn><sn><md>### `delete` vs `purge`

| Command         | Files      | Directories                                    |
| --------------- | ---------- | ---------------------------------------------- |
| `rclone delete` | Deletes | Keeps the main directory                    |
| `rclone purge`  | Deletes | Deletes everything, including the directory |

For example:

```bash
rclone purge mega:Documents
```

&gt; ⚠️ Be careful: depending on your remote's configuration, deleted files may be permanently removed or moved to the provider's trash.
</md></sn>